<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan buys 69,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 69,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taiwan Flour Mills Association bought 69,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat in two shipments at a tender on Thursday, traders said.  </p>
<p>Suppliers Columbia Grain International, Agrex and Mitsui all sold parts of Thursday's shipments.</p>
<p>Both shipments' freight were fixed at US$21.5 per tonne from NFAC, traders said.</p>
<p>Each shipment contains Dark Northern Spring (DNS), Hard Red Winter (HRW) and White Wheat (WW), and all are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest, traders said.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:  Supplier    Type  Tonnes  Delivery Period    Price</p>
<p> Shipment 1		    March 15-April 5</p>
<p>  CGI	  DNS   19,100			   US$191.17</p>
<p>  Agrex	HRW    9,100			   US$185.15</p>
<p>  CGI	   WW    6,800			   US$162.94</p>
<p> Shipment 2		    March 31-April 20</p>
<p>  Mitsui     DNS   18,000			   US$193.00</p>
<p>  Mitsui     HRW    9,400			   US$184.50</p>
<p>  CGI	   WW    6,600			   US$161.89</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-508-0815)</p>
